@startuml
title Physical Room Operational & Housekeeping State Diagram (v0.9.0)

[*] --> Inspected : Room added and verified\n(Hotel Manager)

state "Dirty" as Dirty
state "Clean" as Clean
state "Inspected" as Inspected
state "Out-of-Order" as OOO

Inspected --> Dirty : Guest checks out (FR-CI-03)\n[System / Receptionist]
Clean --> Dirty : Guest checks out / Re-soiled\n[System / Housekeeping]
Dirty --> Clean : Room cleaned\n[Housekeeping Staff]
Clean --> Inspected : Inspection passed\n[Housekeeping Staff / Manager]
Clean --> Dirty : Inspection failed\n[Housekeeping Staff / Manager]

Dirty --> OOO : Maintenance issue reported\n[Housekeeping / Manager]
Clean --> OOO : Maintenance issue reported\n[Housekeeping / Manager]
Inspected --> OOO : Maintenance issue reported\n[Housekeeping / Manager]
OOO --> Dirty : Maintenance completed\n[Hotel Manager / Housekeeping]

note right of Inspected
  **Check-in Readiness Rule (FR-OP-03):**
  Only rooms in **Inspected** state
  (and not currently occupied)
  can be assigned at check-in.
end note

note right of OOO
  **Blocked State (FR-OP-03):**
  Out-of-Order rooms cannot be assigned
  at check-in and are excluded from
  available room-type inventory.
end note

note bottom
  All transitions are validated server-side and logged in
  RoomStatusHistory / AuditEvent (FR-OP-02, NFR-04).
  Note: Operational status is separate from Reservation state.
end note
@enduml
